Sources for `backlog-batch` skill (see plans/skill-audits/backlog-batch.md for the audit):

- Anthropic, "Claude Code best practices" + the Workflow tool (deterministic multi-agent
  orchestration, parallel()/pipeline(), per-agent worktree isolation) — the substrate that
  recovers determinism a long in-session LLM orchestrator would lose.
- git worktrees (native) — per-ticket isolation so parallel file edits never corrupt one
  shared working tree. Composes with superpowers:using-git-worktrees.
- ghuntley "ralph" + gsd-build "get-shit-done" — the deterministic-backpressure and
  thin-orchestrator principles, here applied to a *parallel attended* burst rather than the
  sequential walk-away loop.
- void-harness `autonomous-backlog-loop` — the sister mode; shared Linear-selection and
  craftsman worker-cycle vocabulary, opposite orchestration (process vs subagent) and a
  parallel risk model instead of a sequential one.

Strategy: original (distilled). No single source ships an attended, risk-routed, parallel
ticket drain with worktree isolation and a single reconciled integration PR. We assembled
the Workflow substrate, the worktree isolation, a measured file-overlap partition
(parallel only where the risk is low; sequential for overlap / lockfile / migrations), and
a reconciliation subagent gated by the full suite. The human confirms the plan before
fan-out and owns the PR merge (HITL at the edges).

Deterministic, unit-tested core in the CLI: `selectIndependent` (independent eligible set),
`partition` (risk → parallel/sequential), `buildPlan` (compose), exposed as
`void-harness backlog-batch plan`. The MCP gathering + estimator + fan-out are in-session /
Workflow.

Composes with: brainstorming, source-driven-development, writing-plans, tdd,
commit-discipline, verification-before-completion, using-git-worktrees. Sister of
autonomous-backlog-loop; downstream merge is human-owned (code-review / ship).
